MHD shock diagnostics for the main reconnection phase ($t=36.2\ 	ext{min}$, $y=0\ 	ext{Mm}$), in the same format and notation as Figure 4. Top row: 2D shock diagnostics, displaying (a) the viscous heating $Q_{v}$, (b) the velocity field divergence $ m{
abla}\cdot m{v}$, and (c) the fast-mode Mach number $M_{f}$. Panels (a) and (c) show integral lines of the projection of the magnetic field vector onto the $xz$ plane, while panel (b) shows projected velocity vectors. Middle row: 1D diagnostics along the line segment $L_{1}$, showing: (d) $Q_{v}$, thermal pressure $P$, and magnetic field magnitude $B$; (e) entropy proxy $s$, $M_{f}$, and $ m{
abla}\cdot m{v}$. Bottom row: 1D diagnostics along the line segment $L_{2}$, showing: (f) $Q_{v}$, $P$, and $B$; (g) $s$, $M_{f}$, and $ m{
abla}\cdot m{v}$. The gray bands denote the approximate positions of the two shocks.
